Package: mlcvi
Type: Package
Title: Machine Learning-Based Cultural Values Inventory
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Gary", "Leng",
           email = "gary-h.leng@polyu.edu.hk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "TODO-confirm-or-remove")),
    person("Abhishek", "Sheetal",
           role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "TODO-confirm-or-remove",
                       note = "TODO: confirm role (aut vs ctb) and whether a cph entry is needed"))
  )
Description: Tools for cross-cultural research built around the machine
    learning-based cultural values inventory (ML-CVI) of Leng and Sheetal
    (2025) <doi:10.31235/osf.io/73g8z_v1>: cultural distance between
    countries by the Kogut and Singh (1988) <doi:10.1057/palgrave.jibs.8490394>
    index on Hofstede's dimensions, by a published Shulgin table, and by the
    ML-CVI distance matrix; vectorised lookups for dyadic panel data; Sobel
    (1982) mediation screens of the sixty ML-CVI items; imputation of missing
    country-level indicators by Ridge regression weighted by ML-CVI feature
    importances; and classical distance matrices (Kogut-Singh style,
    Euclidean, Mahalanobis as in Berry, Guillen and Zhou (2010)
    <doi:10.1057/jibs.2010.28>) from user-chosen World Values Survey items,
    pooled or per survey wave.
